const GR_P6A=[
 ["Giving and receiving with あげる, もらう and くれる","Giver が receiver に thing を あげる","あげる (ageru) means that I give something to another person, or that one person gives something to another person. 私は友達に花をあげます means “I give flowers to my friend”. もらう (morau) means that I receive something from another person. The person who gives is marked with に. 私は友達に本をもらいました means “I received a book from my friend”. くれる (kureru) means that another person gives something to me or to my family. 友達が私に本をくれました means “My friend gave me a book”. Do not use あげる when another person gives something to me. Use くれる.",[["友達","tomodachi","friend"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["私","watashi","me"],["に","ni","to"],["本","hon","book"],["を","o","(object)"],["くれました","kuremashita","gave (to me)"],["。","",""]],"My friend gave me a book."],
 ["Doing for someone with てあげる","て-form + あげる","The て-form of a verb plus あげる (ageru) means that you do an action for another person. The person who receives the action is marked with に. 読んであげます means “I read it for you”. The action is a favour that you give. Use it for friends, family and children. Do not use it for a person above you, because it can sound like a favour from a higher person.",[["私","watashi","I"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["弟","otouto","my younger brother"],["に","ni","for"],["本","hon","book"],["を","o","(object)"],["読んで","yonde","read (て-form)"],["あげます","agemasu","do for"],["。","",""]],"I read a book for my younger brother."],
 ["Having someone do it with てもらう","て-form + もらう","The て-form of a verb plus もらう (morau) means that another person does an action for me, and I receive it. The person who does the action is marked with に. 友達に手伝ってもらいました means “My friend helped me”. The speaker is glad that the action was done. It is also used to ask a person to do something: 手伝ってもらいたいです means “I would like you to help”.",[["兄","ani","my older brother"],["に","ni","by"],["荷物","nimotsu","luggage"],["を","o","(object)"],["運んで","hakonde","carry (て-form)"],["もらいました","moraimashita","received"],["。","",""]],"My older brother carried the luggage for me."],
 ["Someone does it for me with てくれる","て-form + くれる","The て-form of a verb plus くれる (kureru) means that another person does an action for me or for my family. The person who does the action is marked with が or は. 友達が手伝ってくれました means “My friend helped me”. The meaning is almost the same as てもらう. With てくれる the person who acts is the subject. With てもらう the person who acts is marked with に.",[["友達","tomodachi","friend"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["部屋","heya","room"],["を","o","(object)"],["掃除して","souji shite","clean (て-form)"],["くれました","kuremashita","did for me"],["。","",""]],"My friend cleaned the room for me."],
 ["Preparing with ておく","て-form + おく","The て-form of a verb plus おく (oku) means that you do an action in advance, for a later purpose. 買っておきます means “I will buy it in advance”. It can also mean that you leave something in that state: ドアを開けておきます means “I leave the door open”. The past is ておきました.",[["旅行","ryokou","trip"],["の","no","’s"],["前","mae","before"],["に","ni","at"],["切符","kippu","ticket"],["を","o","(object)"],["買って","katte","buy (て-form)"],["おきます","okimasu","do in advance"],["。","",""]],"Before the trip, I buy the ticket in advance."]
];
