const GR_P6B=[
 ["Completing or regretting with てしまう","て-form + しまう","The て-form of a verb plus しまう (shimau) has two meanings. The first meaning is that an action is finished completely: 全部食べてしまいました means “I ate everything”. The second meaning is that the speaker regrets something, or that something happened by mistake: 傘を忘れてしまいました means “I forgot my umbrella, unfortunately”. The past is てしまいました.",[["傘","kasa","umbrella"],["を","o","(object)"],["忘れて","wasurete","forget (て-form)"],["しまいました","shimaimashita","did completely"],["。","",""]],"I forgot my umbrella, unfortunately."],
 ["Trying with てみる","て-form + みる","The て-form of a verb plus みる (miru) means to try an action to see what it is like. 食べてみます means “I will try eating it”. Use it for something new. It does not mean “see”. The past 食べてみました means “I tried eating it”.",[["この","kono","this"],["料理","ryouri","dish"],["を","o","(object)"],["食べて","tabete","eat (て-form)"],["みます","mimasu","try"],["。","",""]],"I will try eating this dish."],
 ["Direction of change with ていく and てくる","て-form + いく or くる","The て-form of a verb plus くる (kuru) means that a change has come up to now: 寒くなってきました means “It has become cold”. The same form also means to do something and then come back: 買ってきます means “I will buy it and come back”. The て-form plus いく (iku) means that a change continues from now into the future: 貯まっていきます means “It will keep accumulating”. It also means to do something and then go: 食べていきます means “I eat here and then go”.",[["近頃","chikagoro","these days"],["、","",""],["寒く","samuku","cold (adverb)"],["なって","natte","become (て-form)"],["きました","kimashita","have come to"],["。","",""]],"It has become cold these days."],
 ["Wanting someone to do it with てほしい","Person に + て-form + ほしい","The て-form of a verb plus ほしい (hoshii) means that you want another person to do an action. The person who does the action is marked with に. 兄に手伝ってほしいです means “I want my older brother to help”. For an action that you want to do yourself, use たい. For a thing that you want, use ほしい after the noun: 本がほしいです.",[["兄","ani","my older brother"],["に","ni","(person asked)"],["手伝って","tetsudatte","help (て-form)"],["ほしい","hoshii","want"],["です","desu","is"],["。","",""]],"I want my older brother to help."],
 ["Offering with ましょうか","Verb stem + ましょうか","The verb stem plus ましょうか (mashou ka) means “Shall I …?”. You offer to do something for another person. 荷物を持ちましょうか means “Shall I carry your luggage?”. The answer お願いします means “Yes, please”. The answer 大丈夫です means “No, it is all right”. The same form can also mean “Shall we …?” when you ask someone to do something together.",[["荷物","nimotsu","luggage"],["を","o","(object)"],["持ちましょうか","mochimashou ka","shall I carry"],["。","",""]],"Shall I carry your luggage?"]
];
