const GR_P8A=[
 ["Looks like with そうです","Verb stem or adjective stem + そうです","そうです (sou desu) after a verb stem or an adjective stem means “it looks like …”. You judge by what you see now. 降る becomes 降りそうです (looks like it will fall). 高い becomes 高そうです (looks expensive): take off い first. For a な-adjective, use the stem: 元気そうです (looks healthy). いい becomes よさそうです.",[["雨","ame","rain"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["降りそうです","furisou desu","looks like it will fall"],["。","",""]],"It looks like it will rain."],
 ["I heard that with そうです","Plain form + そうです","そうです (sou desu) after the plain form of a sentence means “I heard that …”. You report what another person or a source said. The plain form is the form without です and ます: 咲く, 咲いた, 高い, 高くない. A noun or a な-adjective needs だ before そうです: 雨だそうです (I heard that it is rain). Compare 降りそうです (it looks like it will rain) and 降るそうです (I heard that it will rain).",[["来週","raishuu","next week"],["桜","sakura","cherry blossoms"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["咲く","saku","bloom"],["そうです","sou desu","I heard that"],["。","",""]],"I heard that the cherry blossoms will bloom next week."],
 ["Seems with ようです","Plain form + ようです","ようです (you desu) after the plain form means “it seems that …”. You think so from what you see, hear or feel, but you are not sure. For a noun, use の: 雨のようです (it seems to be rain). For a な-adjective, use な: 元気なようです (he seems healthy).",[["あの","ano","that"],["ライオン","raion","lion"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["眠い","nemui","sleepy"],["ようです","you desu","seems"],["。","",""]],"That lion seems sleepy."],
 ["Maybe with かもしれません","Plain form + かもしれません","かもしれません (kamoshiremasen) after the plain form means “maybe …”. The chance is not high. A noun or a な-adjective has no だ before かもしれません: 雨かもしれません (maybe it is rain), 有名かもしれません (maybe he is famous). Use でしょう when you are more sure.",[["あの","ano","that"],["俳優","haiyuu","actor"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["有名","yuumei","famous"],["かもしれません","kamoshiremasen","may be"],["。","",""]],"That actor may be famous."],
 ["Should be with はずです","Plain form + はずです","はずです (hazu desu) after the plain form means “it should be …”. You expect it from a reason that you know. For a noun, use の: 休みのはずです. For a な-adjective, use な: 便利なはずです. Do not use it for things you only hope.",[["パソコン","pasokon","computer"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["机","tsukue","desk"],["の","no","of"],["上","ue","top"],["に","ni","on"],["ある","aru","is"],["はずです","hazu desu","should be"],["。","",""]],"The computer should be on the desk."]
];
