const GR_P14B=[
 ["Full of with だらけ","Noun + だらけ","だらけ (darake) after a noun means that the place or thing is full of that noun. It usually means something that you do not like. 部屋はごみだらけです means “the room is full of rubbish”.",[["部屋","heya","room"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["ごみ","gomi","rubbish"],["だらけ","darake","full of"],["です","desu","is"],["。","",""]],"The room is full of rubbish."],
 ["Having a tendency with っぽい","Noun or verb stem + っぽい","っぽい (ppoi) after a noun means “has the look or the feel of that noun”. 子供っぽい means “childish”. After a verb stem it means “tends to”. 忘れっぽい means “tends to forget”. It is often used for something that you do not like. っぽい is an い-adjective: 子供っぽくないです means “is not childish”.",[["弟","otouto","my younger brother"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["少し","sukoshi","a little"],["子供っぽい","kodomoppoi","childish"],["です","desu","is"],["。","",""]],"My younger brother is a little childish."],
 ["Tend to with がちです","Verb stem or noun + がちです","がち (gachi) after a verb stem or a noun means that something often happens in a way that is not good. 遅れがちです means “tends to be late”. 病気がちです means “is often ill”. It describes a tendency, not one single event.",[["朝","asa","in the morning"],["、","",""],["遅れがち","okuregachi","tend to be late"],["です","desu","am"],["。","",""]],"I tend to be late in the morning."],
 ["Judging from with ことから","Plain form + ことから","ことから (koto kara) after a plain form says what you saw or found as the reason for a conclusion: “judging from the fact that …”. The conclusion comes after it. Use と思います to say what you think.",[["靴","kutsu","shoes"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["玄関","genkan","entrance hall"],["に","ni","in"],["ある","aru","are"],["ことから","koto kara","judging from the fact that"],["、","",""],["けん","Ken","Ken (name)"],["は","wa","(topic)"],["家","ie","home"],["に","ni","at"],["いる","iru","is"],["と思います","to omoimasu","I think"],["。","",""]],"Judging from the fact that the shoes are in the entrance hall, I think Ken is at home."],
 ["Because, as a polite excuse, with ものですから","Plain form + ものですから","ものですから (mono desu kara) after a plain form gives a reason in a polite and soft way. It is often an excuse or an explanation for something that went wrong. It is more polite than から. The result is usually in the past.",[["すみません","sumimasen","I am sorry"],["、","",""],["電車","densha","train"],["が","ga","(subject)"],["遅れた","okureta","was late"],["ものですから","mono desu kara","because"],["、","",""],["遅く","osoku","late"],["なりました","narimashita","became"],["。","",""]],"I am sorry. Because the train was late, I became late."]
];
